ew variable $u={x}^{3}+2.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{x}^{2}{5}^{{x}^{3}+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4\\cdot {5}^{{x}^{3}+2}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int {5}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\int {5}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\frac{{5}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot {5}^{{x}^{3}+2}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679317 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eec4844d-544c-5a57-b89c-ee1bd78d81e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\frac{5^{2 - x^{3}}}{\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eec4844d-544c-5a57-b89c-ee1bd78d81e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\frac{5^{2 - x^{3}}}{\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679415} :answer-field/id #uuid "765fc159-0cc3-5241-954f-661bc69482ee" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679360}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "06647049-685d-571a-8830-feba3fbdbb67" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 4 \\cdot 5^{2 - x^{3}} x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int 5^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\frac{5^{u}}{\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 - x^{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(- 3 x^{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 4 \\cdot 5^{2 - x^{3}} x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int 5^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int 5^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\