ion rule:\n\n$$\n\\int 2^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\frac{2^{u}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int 2^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\frac{2^{u}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 \\cdot 2^{x^{3} + 2}}{3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2042cd43-aab5-5e29-bdf4-614c1ea3eff1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{\\frac{x^{3}}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}}}{3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691317} {:answer/id #uuid "291c5943-96df-5d10-9847-480ba9dcddbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3} + 1+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691319} {:answer/id #uuid "39387465-0e87-5704-a1c8-1b1ad04bbc29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x^{3} + 1}}{6 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691324} {:answer/id #uuid "bdb0dd4b-eeea-5f7c-b1ab-c6f7d800e244" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x^{3} + 1}}{3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691354} {:answer/id #uuid "ded207fb-cb56-58eb-9a0f-d658894755b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x^{3} + 1}}{9 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdb0dd4b-eeea-5f7c-b1ab-c6f7d800e244" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x^{3} + 1}}{3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691354} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffe4f4f3-37ec-5331-b8dd-d208cf268e9d" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691364}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c3d97b0-c388-5846-b671-21162ba60fb3" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 2^{x^{3} + 1} x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x^{3} + 1$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(3 x^{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 2^{x^{3} + 1} x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int 2^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int 2^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\frac{2^{u}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int 2^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\frac{2^{u}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2^{x^{3} + 1}}{3 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186691362 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ae61529-6805-52b3-872c-2cce02eae907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9 \\cdot 3^{x^{2}}}{2 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691343} {:answer/id #uuid "96b393ba-962a-542a-8a26-a11436b41bae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\cdot 3^{x}}{2 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691348} {:answer/id #uuid "da17c905-18be-587f-bafd-d0593b67804c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691359} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf6f19b-b286-53dd-beeb-b62f689ebc47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\cdot 3^{x^{2}}}{2 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691361} {:answer/id #uuid "f8c4fa70-69ff-5666-b0ee-a64ecc64d96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\cdot 3^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}}}{2 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ecf6f19b-b286-53dd-beeb-b62f689ebc47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\cdot 3^{x^{2}}}{2 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691361} :answer-field/id #uuid "03f80d55-71ea-5f0f-a492-b6cf5313b7a5" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186691310}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f755098d-0436-563b-a5bd-55634d7a5b27" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 3 \\cdot 3^{x^{2}} x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x^{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(2 x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 3 \\cdot 3^{x^{2}} x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int 3^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int 3^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\frac{3^{u}}{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}+C.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int 3^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\frac{3^{u}}{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3 \\cdot 3^{x^{2}}}{2 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}+C.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Products Containing Other Exponential Functions"}]}
